    {
      "id": "claim_c444c647ee704c44ab1f669a0b624344",
      "statement": "The background dispatcher auto-starts only when opted in: the plugin register() runs _should_auto_start_dispatcher(), which passes only when ZEROFACTORY_SKIP_DISPATCHER / ZEROFACTORY_DISABLE_DISPATCHER are unset, zerofactory.db exists, and the auto_start_dispatcher setting (default false) is enabled; it then runs init_db(), ensure_builtin_cron_jobs(), and start_background_dispatcher(). dashboard/routes/dispatch.py additionally exposes explicit operator control: POST /dispatch/start (gated on profile readiness), POST /dispatch/stop, GET /dispatch/status, and GET /health/stuck-tasks.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://__init__.py#L252-L288",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a881d2cddc25bb1913c19aa21e137b54608f97e02c8113a961d3999b4e76d5ee:"
        }
